I believe this delay is related to when balance receives requests to create or capture orders from rentals.

Logs which demonstrate all three orders when they reach commerce-gateway and balance-user are [here|http://kibana.internal/app/kibana#/discover?_g=(refreshInterval:(display:Off,pause:!f,value:0),time:(from:'2022-05-17T11:16:40.000Z',mode:absolute,to:'2022-05-17T11:23:00.000Z'))&_a=(columns:!(node.log_level,node.log_message,node_from.service_id,node.service_id,node.path,node_root.hash,query.additional_params),filters:!(('$state':(store:appState),meta:(alias:!n,disabled:!f,index:'logs-nodejs-*',key:node.code_owner,negate:!f,type:phrase,value:balance),query:(match:(node.code_owner:(query:balance,type:phrase))))),index:'logs-nodejs-*',interval:auto,query:(query_string:(analyze_wildcard:!t,query:'%22source_id:%20118282001%22%20OR%20%22source_id:%20118282554%22%20OR%20%22bookingKey.source_id:%20118282001%22%20OR%20%22bookingKey.source_id:%20118283170%22%20OR%22bookingKey.source_id:%20118282554%22')),sort:!('@timestamp',desc))].

Order of what happened:
1) First order creation request received at {{14:16:43.730}}

2) Second order creation request received at {{14:19:45.578}}. Here we don’t know first order ended.

3) First order capture request received at {{14:19:45.969}}

4) Third order creation request received at {{14:22:45.824}}. Here we know first order ended, but not second.

5) Second order capture request received at {{14:22:50.832}}

Now these are *not* nginx logs (which would show exactly when commerce received request from business line) so theoretically there might be some time passing between when request is received, some logic applied and then log is produced but tbh I don’t think this is issue in this particular case. It is because same latency applies to all logs.

TL;DR I think the delay is on rentals side. They are asking us to authorise new order before capturing previous.

