In {{13:18:55}} the log is interrupted, so we don’t know what happened with the call on the device based on the attached log, however we’re able to trace it in mixpanel. 

* Another push message is received in 50 seconds after the call was accepted. There are no traces in Mixpanel that the previous call was finished and what finish reason was there. A push message is for a call with call_id {{46598C0B-05FE-4660-8770-6FA9B4D8C76A}} but the caller is the same (the calls are associated with the same order_id = {{889724239}}). 

{noformat}1:19:24 pm, Thu, Apr 28, 2022 -> VoIP Notification Received for call_id = 46598C0B-05FE-4660-8770-6FA9B4D8C76A{noformat}

* The call with session_id {{46598C0B-05FE-4660-8770-6FA9B4D8C76A}} ends with incoming call error, so a second instance of  {{SinchClient}} is not even created

{noformat}1:19:24 pm, Thu, Apr 28, 2022 -> Incoming Call Error (IllegalVoipRepoStateException: was in AcceptedCall, but expected idle){noformat}

* 10 seconds after receiving a seconds push user tapped {{End Call}} button end finished the call, so the button at this point is probably available as well. Call ID is not reported in this event (while it can be reported if present) which means it’s {{null}} and which probably indicates that a current call instance was erased in {{SinchCallRepository.}} Most probably it happened after {{Incoming Call Error }} as there is a special handling for releasing an active {{SinchClient}} that also erases the current call reference.

{noformat}1:19:35 pm, Thu, Apr 28, 2022 -> End Call Tap for order id = 889724239, call_id is not reported{noformat}

* Call finished with a reason {{CANCELED}}.  Call ID is not reported either while it can be reported if present.

{noformat}1:19:35 pm, Thu, Apr 28, 2022 -> Call Finished for order_id = 889724239, call_id is not reported{noformat}

I would assume that in this very moment a current call state in {{SinchCallRepository}} is messed up and this is what made Accept and Reject buttons disappear.



There is a difference with [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CLIENTAPP-14305|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CLIENTAPP-14305|smart-link] because in this case there is no race condition and the second incoming call push message was arrived 50 seconds after the first one, though the fact that the inconsistency in the call state was caused by two incoming call pushes received from a single user while the call from the first session wasn’t finished properly makes me think that they are related and the fix would require complete revisiting of the internal call state managing same as in this referenced ticket.

So I’m closing this one as a duplicate and we’ll proceed monitoring if a similar case come up once again. Sinch couldn’t help us to understand why two pushes were sent in the first place because they don’t keep logs on the backend for such a long time. Hopefully when we receive a similar report they could help us understanding this.

